 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Great. Questions really give the interview back to the guest. Stick to one question at a time, and keep it few lines long if you write it down. Sure. I asked a famous musician about the moment they knew they'd made it, and they told me about a small hall with a packed room. Keep it to about four minutes so your guest isn't bored, and give them a nice place to breathe. Get their permission first, so they don't get excited and say too much. A quick email checks all the bases. You' welcome. Enjoy the interview. Asking good questions is a great skill to have.",
